// What each country was, in the figures that decide how its regions are built.
//
// Loaded after 00_countries.json and before the population is dealt out, because these are
// inputs to that arithmetic rather than corrections to it: how urban a country is decides
// what trades its regions hold, and how much of it works the land sets the level the curve
// could only guess at.
//
//   literacy      share of adults who can read
//   urbanisation  share living in towns
//   agriculture   share of the workforce on the land
//
// Rounded 2020s figures from the usual international sources. A country that is not listed
// has all three worked out from what it earns per head, which is a decent guess and never
// as good as a real number - so the honest way to improve this game's statistics is to add
// countries to this file, not to tune the curve.
//
// Everything else about a country - money, army, politics - stays in 00_countries.json.
